    "result_text": "All tests green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and its 3 postcode cases all pass, along with a clean full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented an optional, region-validated `postcode` for owners across the OfficeFloor create/update pipelines.\n\n**Validation rule** \u2014 new function step `ValidateOwnerPostcode` (wired into both `owners.POST.yml` and `{ownerId}.PUT.yml`):\n- Absent/blank postcode \u2192 accepted (optional, backward-compatible).\n- Present but not exactly 4 digits \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n- Present, 4 digits, city has a known region (via existing `Localities`) but out of that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 **400**.\n- Present, 4 digits, city with no known region \u2192 accepted (permissive default).\n\n**Store & return:**\n- `Owner` entity: new `postcode` column + getter/setter.\n- `openapi.yml`: added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` bind it on request and emit it on response; MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT) now copies `postcode` onto the entity.\n\n**Supporting pieces:**\n- `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` (400 with `errors: [\"postcode\"]`) + escalation YAML.\n- Added the `postcode` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n- The hsqldb seed `data.sql` used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, which the new column broke \u2014 converted those 10 rows to column-qualified inserts (matching how h2's data.sql already works), so column order/count is no longer brittle.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: I placed all postcode validation in a dedicated pipeline step rather than as an OpenAPI bean-validation `pattern`, because the create pipeline's first step binds `@RequestBody` without `@Valid`, and the out-of-range check is inherently a business rule that depends on the city's region \u2014 not expressible as a static field pattern.",
